## What to deliver

Build and rig the Repeater up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png` matches
the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together correctly, and the
rig is complete: a slim brass post founded on the ground, a rotating drum of many short iron
barrels at the top, and a contiguous verdigris accent collar where the drum meets the post
sculpted **only** in `#2f7d72` and appearing nowhere else on the model. **Author the two
required animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation subcommands: an **`idle`**
(the drum ticking over slowly and continuously on its own, post and base fixed) and a
**`fire`** (the drum spinning up fast and cycling its barrels in a rapid burst, post and base
fixed). The animations and the accent region are the fixed contract — produce all of them;
the parts and joints that realize them are yours. You may add your own extra parts, joints,
or animations on top, but do not drop or contradict the required `idle` and `fire`. Before
you finish, run `voxel-anim render` so it emits the per-part `.glb` geometry your result is
built from — an unrendered part is scored as empty (`voxel-anim render --component <part>`
redraws one part; `voxel-anim render --time <ms> --animation <name>` renders the model posed
at that instant of an animation to check the motion). When you are satisfied, stop: the
recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
